# Compiled Adventure documents (`packs[].prebuilt` in package-build.config.yaml).
# These fourteen files are the module's shipped compendium source, written by
# the Foundry compendium tooling rather than by hand — `content-build package
# unpack` emits them with `JSON.stringify(…, null, 2)`, the 2-space indent every
# HeroicLands repository's pack JSON shares. The shared Prettier configuration
# is `tabWidth: 4`, so formatting them would put the two writers permanently at
# odds: every re-extract would revert the format and re-redden the check.
#
# The churn is not small either. Prettier rewrites the *smallest* of the
# fourteen from 306 KB to 388 KB (+26%) and restructures its line breaks; across
# all fourteen that is ~430,000 lines, essentially every one of them, burying
# any real content change in review and in `git blame` forever.
#
# Same rule, same reason as `**/packs` in Song-of-Heroic-Lands-FoundryVTT and
# `assets/manifests/*.json` in sohl-thalorna and harn-ensemble: machine-written
# JSON belongs to the tool that writes it. Prettier owns the prose here.
assets/packs/
